# Operator-level dispatch: verify that [+ a b] dispatches through the Addable
# instance for Dict-typed values (non-Int/Float fast path).
#
# This test relies on the operator dispatch mechanism added in the operator-dispatch
# sprint: builtin_add falls through to try_dispatch_method("Addable", ...) after
# the Int/Float fast path. Addable instance method calls [builtin-add] (pure,
# no re-dispatch) so there is no infinite recursion.
#
# The instance wraps dict values with an `n:` field. [+ s1 s2] dispatches to
# the Dict/Dict Addable arm, which adds the inner n: fields and returns a new dict.

[
  make-scale: [fn [let n] [n: n]]

  _: [instance Addable
    [let a@Dict b@Dict c]: [+: [fn [let x y] [make-scale [+ [get x n] [get y n]]]]]]

  s1: [make-scale 3]
  s2: [make-scale 4]
]
[get [+ s1 s2] n]
=== error
[E013] no instance for Addable (Dict, Dict) (defined at 20:6-20:15)
  in [+ ...] at 20:6-20:15
  in [builtin-get ...] at stdlib/prelude.llt:843:25-843:47
   |
  843 | """] [let key@k dict@d] [builtin-get key dict]]
      |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  in [get ...] at 20:1-20:18

